PATCH 506: the ammo-count and READY/LOADING HUD plates (82a1, 82ee).

Two more 209e paint methods with the family defect: BX is the display-list element's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET
and BP the walk base (the walk publishes BX to DGROUP:0x3e08 and BP to g_fist_paintbp, patch 142), and
DAT_2000_2d34 is the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET (patch 300).  Both were dereferenced as host pointers.

FUN_0000_82a1 (asm 0x82a1-0x82ed), the ammo-count plate:
    82a2: mov si,[bx+2] ; 82a5: movzbw bx,[bp+si+1]     ; the weapon-station index
    82a9: add bx,[0x6d34] ; 82ad: mov ax,[bx+0xad]      ; the PLAYER's per-station ammo WORD
    82b1: pop bx ; push ax ; lea bx,[bx+4]
    82b6: mov ax,[bx] ; mov bx,[bx+2] ; lcall 0f69:5c41 ; 52d1(x,y)
    82c0: mov ax,2 ; lcall 0f69:5bbe                    ; 524e(2)
    82c8: mov al,0x4f ; lcall 0f69:5c7b                 ; 530b, AH = 524e's high byte
    82cf: mov si,0x96ac ; lcall 0f69:5e9b               ; thunk_5531 over DGROUP:0x96ac
    82d7: mov al,0xe ; lcall 0f69:5c7b                  ; 530b with the SAME AH -- only AL is reloaded
    82de: pop ax ; mov si,0x1f8c ; call 0x2c5           ; format the ammo count into DGROUP:0x1f8c
    82e5: mov si,0x1f8d ; lcall 0f69:5e9b
Four defects: the element host-deref'd; the entire ammo lookup dropped, with 02c5 handed the CS artifact
0xf69 as the value to format; thunk_5531 (which takes a HOST pointer, patch 139) passed the raw near
offset 0x96ac; and the uninitialised `extraout_AH` used for the second 530b although the asm reloads
only AL.

FUN_0000_82ee (asm 0x82ee-0x8328), the READY/LOADING plate: same element base-loss, the player near
offset host-deref'd in `cmpb [di+0xa8],0` (the reload timer that picks LOADING over READY), and the AL=0
argument of the `lcall [0x60a]` dropped.  This was the top SIGSEGV of the post-505 sweep
(82ee <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a).
